# PITCH mirrors and the two directions mean opposite things, YAW does
# not mirror, ROLL mirrors. That is the whole scope argument: the fix
# touches pitch and nothing else.
#
# PART 2 -- the three gestures at their own peaks, off the shipped
# table. The peak is found by stepping t in 1ms over the gesture and
# taking the largest |hp|, with p and env computed exactly as the
# engine's loop computes them (p = t / dur, gestureEnvelope(t, dur, 0)).
#
nod  dur 0.9s  peak |hp| at 274ms
    vroid-sample-b        hp  -0.1078  sx   0.0000  ey   0.000  eye toward face     5.97mm  eye dY    -3.52mm  head toward face     0.00mm
    vrm1-twist-sample     hp   0.1078  sx   0.0000  ey   0.000  eye toward face     6.61mm  eye dY    -2.67mm  head toward face     0.00mm
    vroid-studio-dressup  hp   0.1078  sx   0.0000  ey   0.000  eye toward face     6.61mm  eye dY    -2.67mm  head toward face     0.00mm

bounce  dur 1.2s  peak |hp| at 600ms
    vroid-sample-b        hp  -0.0500  sx  -0.0500  ey   0.000  eye toward face    25.09mm  eye dY    -2.69mm  head toward face    19.54mm
    vrm1-twist-sample     hp   0.0500  sx   0.0500  ey   0.000  eye toward face    27.49mm  eye dY    -0.95mm  head toward face    21.35mm
    vroid-studio-dressup  hp   0.0500  sx   0.0500  ey   0.000  eye toward face    27.49mm  eye dY    -0.95mm  head toward face    21.35mm

toeLook  dur 2s  peak |hp| at 1000ms
    vroid-sample-b        hp  -0.3000  sx   0.0000  ey  -2.000  eye toward face    15.54mm  eye dY   -11.31mm  head toward face     0.00mm
    vrm1-twist-sample     hp   0.3000  sx   0.0000  ey  -2.000  eye toward face    17.55mm  eye dY    -9.13mm  head toward face     0.00mm
    vroid-studio-dressup  hp   0.3000  sx   0.0000  ey  -2.000  eye toward face    17.55mm  eye dY    -9.13mm  head toward face     0.00mm

# Every family reads the same sign on every row, which is the point:
# one gesture, one meaning, on a body that faces either way.
